@startuml
title F12 - Acknowledgement and resolution
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Primary caregiver" as Caregiver
boundary "A04\nApp incidents" as A04
control "B04\nIncident workflow" as B04
control "B05\nNotification routing" as B05
control "B07\nRead models/API" as B07
control "H08\nHub cloud link" as H08
Caregiver -> A04: Open incident and request claim
A04 -> B04: POST claim with idempotency key
B04 -> B04: Acquire bounded owner lease; reject competing live owner
Caregiver -> A04: Acknowledge after taking responsibility
A04 -> B04: POST acknowledge
B04 -> B05: Stop still-pending escalation jobs
B04 -> B07: Publish acknowledged state
B07 -> H08: Optionally return caregiver action for hub visibility
Caregiver -> A04: Resolve with explicit outcome after contact/check
A04 -> B04: POST resolve; closed transition is auditable
note over B05,A04: Provider acceptance never equals human acknowledgement or incident resolution.
note over Caregiver,H08: Outcome - Ownership, acknowledgement and resolution are distinct idempotent transitions with bounded concurrency.
@enduml
